# Document / Tab Titles

Every screen must set a professional browser tab title. Do not leave the Vite default (`2h-central-hub-production`) or a blank/stale title after navigation.

## Format

```
{Page} · 2H Central Hub
```

- **Page** — short human label (Title Case): `Dashboard`, `Clients`, `Create Client`, `Sign In`.
- **Suffix** — always `· 2H Central Hub` (via shared helper; do not hardcode the brand string in pages).
- Optional detail when useful: `Edit Client · Acme Corp · 2H Central Hub` (keep under ~60 chars when possible).

## How

- Use `useDocumentTitle` from `@/hooks` (or `<DocumentTitle title="…" />` from `@/components/common`).
- Set the title in the **page** (or shared layout that owns the screen), not deep inside random leaf widgets.
- New routes: add a title when you add the page — never ship a route without one.

## Tone

- Full meaning at a glance; concise; no slang, no `page`, no raw path segments (`/clients/new`).
- Prefer names that match the in-page heading.

## Examples

| Route | Tab title |
|-------|-----------|
| `/auth/sign-in` | `Sign In · 2H Central Hub` |
| `/dashboard` | `Dashboard · 2H Central Hub` |
| `/clients` | `Clients · 2H Central Hub` |
| `/clients/new` | `Create Client · 2H Central Hub` |
| `/clients/:id/edit` | `Edit Client · 2H Central Hub` |
| `/admin` | `Admin · 2H Central Hub` |
